# Paths trufflehog skips, each with its reason. Nothing here is listed to
# quieten a scan.
#
# Build output and the object database are not source. Git history is scanned
# separately and properly by gitleaks, which understands commits; pointing a
# filesystem scanner at .git/objects just re-reads every historical blob as if
# it were a file on disk.
^\.git/
^target/
^app/src-tauri/target/
#
# The connector-URL fixture: a URL carrying embedded user info, pointing at a
# reserved and unresolvable `.example` name. The test asserts the user
# info is discarded before the asset identity is built. Removing it would be a
# bug, not a fix.
^crates/topgent-core/tests/suite/inventory\.rs$
